# Line endings: LF everywhere, in the repo AND in the working copy.
#
# This project is edited on Windows, but everything that consumes the files is
# Linux: `make` runs in a container that mounts this folder at
# /mnt/cctv_app, and rpi/*.py is scp'd to the Pi. Windows git defaults
# to core.autocrlf=true, which would hand those consumers a CRLF working copy
# and break the shebangs ("bad interpreter: No such file or directory") in
# opencv_cross/build_opencv.sh and the Pi scripts. Pinning eol=lf here overrides
# each developer's autocrlf setting, so the rule travels with the repo.
* text=auto eol=lf

# Binary assets — never convert, never diff as text.
*.png  binary
*.jpg  binary
*.jpeg binary
*.gif  binary
*.ico  binary
*.ttf  binary
*.cap  binary
*.crt  binary
*.key  binary
